…@lower-…@engine-…"},{"id":"spn-47159","text":" sealed + closes"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-33111","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-47160","text":"3. A real emitted episode — "},{"id":"spn-47161","marks":["code"],"text":"examples/eval-one/episodes/episode-<id>/"}]},{"id":"blk-33112","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47162","text":"A committed, five-signal 1.0 episode you can "},{"id":"spn-47163","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs verify-episode"},{"id":"spn-47164","text":" directly. Emitted by:"}]},{"id":"blk-33113","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"$ trvs eval-one examples/eval-one/residency-forge --output examples/eval-one/episodes \\\n      --platform linux-x86_64 -- python3 $PWD/test/fixtures/residency_agent.py\n  status ✓ ok · reward 1 · bundle …/episode-e125d77b…f415\n$ trvs verify-episode examples/eval-one/episodes/episode-e125d77b…f415\n  closure ✓ · artifacts ✓ · citations/patch/tests/identity/finding_completeness ✓\n  reward ✓ (1.0) · episode-id ✓ · verified ✓ closed"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33115","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47165","marks":["bold"],"text":"Note on the id:"},{"id":"spn-47166","text":" "},{"id":"spn-47167","marks":["code"],"text":"residency-forge"},{"id":"spn-47168","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-47169","marks":["code"],"text":"task_id"},{"id":"spn-47170","text":" bakes the acceptance command's absolute "},{"id":"spn-47171","marks":["code"],"text":"argv[0]"},{"id":"spn-47172","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-47173","marks":["code"],"text":"sys.executable"},{"id":"spn-47174","text":") — see the prior memo §6.3 — so the emitted "},{"id":"spn-47175","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-<id>"},{"id":"spn-47176","text":" is environment-specific and will differ on your machine. The "},{"id":"spn-47177","marks":["italic"],"text":"shape"},{"id":"spn-47178","text":" and closure are what to review; a fresh "},{"id":"spn-47179","marks":["code"],"text":"--output"},{"id":"spn-47180","text":" run on your box reproduces the same structure with your interpreter's path."}]}],"id":"blk-33114","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-33116","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-47181","text":"4. Reclassification you asked me to record"}]},{"id":"blk-33117","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47182","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-47183","marks":["code"],"text":"residency-forge"},{"id":"spn-47184","text":" bundle is a "},{"id":"spn-47185","marks":["bold"],"text":"five-signal conformance fixture"},{"id":"spn-47186","text":" — it exercises the full citations/patch/tests/identity contract deterministically via the stub agent. It is "},{"id":"spn-47187","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-47188","text":" a genuine Evidence Residency "},{"id":"spn-47189","marks":["italic"],"text":"finding"},{"id":"spn-47190","text":" about real code: the \"spec\" and \"src\" are minimal fixtures chosen to make each signal's pass/fail path reachable and byte-reproducible. Treat every reward/verdict in the examples + batteries as a "},{"id":"spn-47191","marks":["bold"],"text":"contract-conformance"},{"id":"spn-47192","text":" demonstration, not a substantive spec-vs-impl result. The first genuine spec/impl task (real repo, real finding) remains future work, gated behind TestPlanV2 + portable toolchain refs (below)."}]},{"id":"blk-33118","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-47193","text":"5. New autonomous decisions — please ratify or steer"}]},{"id":"blk-33119","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47194","text":"None move a content-addressed identity beyond Req 3 ("},{"id":"spn-47195","marks":["code"],"text":"verification_evidence"},{"id":"spn-47196","text":" into the allowlist) and Req 7 (the version-string widening) — both of which your ruling directed."}]},{"id":"blk-33120","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33122","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47197","marks":["bold"],"text":"Saved evidence files are re-checked against the receipt digest on verify."},{"id":"spn-47198","text":" The"}]}],"id":"blk-33121","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-33123","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47199","text":"ruling's replay check compares the "},{"id":"spn-47200","marks":["italic"],"text":"re-run"},{"id":"spn-47201","text":" verifier's digest to the receipt; I also added a check that the "},{"id":"spn-47202","marks":["bold"],"text":"persisted"},{"id":"spn-47203","text":" "},{"id":"spn-47204","marks":["code"],"text":"verifiers/<sig>.json"},{"id":"spn-47205","text":" bytes hash to the receipt digest, so tampering the kept file is caught even if the replay happens to reproduce the same state. (This is what "},{"id":"spn-47206","marks":["code"],"text":"tampered_verifier_evidence_file_rejected"},{"id":"spn-47207","text":" pins.) Say the word if you'd rather the saved file be treated as purely decorative."}]},{"id":"blk-33124","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33126","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47208","marks":["bold"],"text":"Runtime tamper (`policy_violations`) is not recomputed on replay."},{"id":"spn-47209","text":" A write-escape"}]}],"id":"blk-33125","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-33127","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47210","text":"is a "},{"id":"spn-47211","marks":["italic"],"text":"live-run observation"},{"id":"spn-47212","text":" not recoverable from a digest; replay scores the un-tampered path, and a saved receipt that lies about a tampered reward is caught by the episode-id self-consistency check ("},{"id":"spn-47213","marks":["code"],"text":"tampered_receipt_reward_rejected"},{"id":"spn-47214","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-33128","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33130","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47215","marks":["bold"],"text":"`--json` prints the receipt to stdout; the bundle path goes to stderr."},{"id":"spn-47216","text":" Keeps the"}]}],"id":"blk-33129","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-33131","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47217","text":"stdout contract (a pure episode receipt) byte-identical whether or not "},{"id":"spn-47218","marks":["code"],"text":"--output"},{"id":"spn-47219","text":" is set."}]},{"id":"blk-33132","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33134","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47220","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-47221","marks":["code"],"text":"verify-episode"},{"id":"spn-47222","text":" wires "},{"id":"spn-47223","marks":["code"],"text":"tests"},{"id":"spn-47224","text":" unconditionally and "},{"id":"spn-47225","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-47226","text":" when the engine is"}]}],"id":"blk-33133","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-33135","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47227","text":"locatable.** An engine-less box that verifies a bundle which scored "},{"id":"spn-47228","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-47229","text":" gets an honest signal "},{"id":"spn-47230","marks":["italic"],"text":"mismatch"},{"id":"spn-47231","text":" (never a false pass), plus a stderr warn."}]},{"id":"blk-33136","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33138","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47232","marks":["bold"],"text":"The manifest carries a non-canonical `created_at`."},{"id":"spn-47233","text":" Wall-clock provenance only;"}]}],"id":"blk-33137","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":5},{"id":"blk-33139","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47234","text":"it is outside every id and never read on verify."}]},{"id":"blk-33140","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-47235","text":"6. Future (NOT started — awaiting your steer)"}]},{"id":"blk-33141","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-47236","text":"In the order you set: "},{"id":"spn-47237","marks":["bold"],"text":"TestPlanV2 + portable toolchain refs"},{"id":"spn-47238","text":" → the "},{"id":"spn-47239","marks":["bold"],"text":"first genuine spec/impl task"},{"id":"spn-47240","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-47241","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs compare"},{"id":"spn-47242","text":